msgid ""
"# SLSTR VIS/SWIR Bands (S1–S6)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) captures "
"Top-of-Atmosphere radiances in six solar reflective channels at 500 m "
"resolution: S1 (0.555 µm, vegetation/aerosol), S2 (0.659 µm, NDVI/aerosol), "
"S3 (0.865 µm, NDVI/cloud flagging), S4 (1.375 µm, cirrus detection), S5 "
"(1.61 µm, ice/snow/vegetation), and S6 (2.25 µm, vegetation state). Each "
"band is available in nadir and oblique views, enabling dual-angle "
"observation of land and ocean surfaces. The L1B product contains "
"geolocated, calibrated radiances produced by signal calibration, "
"re-gridding, and cloud flagging.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."
msgstr ""
"# Kanali SLSTR VIS/SWIR (S1–S6)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) zajema "
"sevanja na vrhu atmosfere v šestih kanalih odbitega sončnega sevanja z "
"ločljivostjo 500 m: S1 (0,555 µm, vegetacija/aerosoli), S2 (0,659 µm, "
"NDVI/aerosoli), S3 (0,865 µm, NDVI/označevanje oblakov), S4 (1,375 µm, "
"zaznavanje cirusov), S5 (1,61 µm, led/sneg/vegetacija) in S6 (2,25 µm, "
"stanje vegetacije). Vsak kanal je na voljo v nadirnem in poševnem pogledu, "
"kar omogoča opazovanje kopenskih in oceanskih površin pod dvema kotoma. "
"Izdelek L1B vsebuje geolocirana, kalibrirana sevanja, pridobljena s "
"kalibracijo signala, ponovnim vzorčenjem na mrežo in označevanjem oblakov.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."

msgid ""
"# SLSTR Thermal Infrared Bands (S7–S9)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) captures "
"Top-of-Atmosphere brightness temperatures in three thermal infrared "
"channels at 1 km resolution: S7 (3.74 µm, sea/land surface temperature and "
"fire detection), S8 (10.85 µm, sea/land surface temperature and fire "
"detection), and S9 (12.0 µm, sea/land surface temperature). Each band is "
"available in nadir and oblique views, enabling dual-angle observation for "
"improved atmospheric correction and surface temperature retrieval. The L1B "
"product contains geolocated, calibrated brightness temperatures produced by "
"signal calibration, re-gridding, and cloud flagging.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."
msgstr ""
"# Termalni infrardeči kanali SLSTR (S7–S9)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) zajema "
"svetlostne temperature na vrhu atmosfere v treh termalnih infrardečih "
"kanalih z ločljivostjo 1 km: S7 (3,74 µm, temperatura morskega/kopenskega "
"površja in zaznavanje požarov), S8 (10,85 µm, temperatura "
"morskega/kopenskega površja in zaznavanje požarov) in S9 (12,0 µm, "
"temperatura morskega/kopenskega površja). Vsak kanal je na voljo v nadirnem "
"in poševnem pogledu, kar omogoča opazovanje pod dvema kotoma za boljši "
"atmosferski popravek in pridobivanje temperature površja. Izdelek L1B "
"vsebuje geolocirane, kalibrirane svetlostne temperature, pridobljene s "
"kalibracijo signala, ponovnim vzorčenjem na mrežo in označevanjem oblakov.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."

msgid ""
"# Tristimulus\n"
"\n"
"The colours of natural waters differ markedly across the globe, depending "
"on water composition and illumination conditions. Ocean colour instruments "
"measure water-leaving radiance in narrow spectral bands to retrieve "
"water-quality indicators. The true colour of natural waters is derived by "
"calculating tristimulus values — the three primaries (X, Y, Z) that specify "
"a colour stimulus as perceived by the human eye.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/tristimulus/)."
msgstr ""
"# Tristimulus\n"
"\n"
"Barve naravnih voda se po svetu močno razlikujejo glede na sestavo vode in "
"osvetlitvene razmere. Instrumenti za barvo oceanov merijo sevanje, ki "
"zapušča vodo, v ozkih spektralnih kanalih, da pridobijo kazalnike kakovosti "
"vode. Prava barva naravnih voda se izpelje z izračunom tristimulusnih "
"vrednosti – treh primarnih vrednosti (X, Y, Z), ki določajo barvni "
"dražljaj, kot ga zaznava človeško oko.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/tristimulus/)."

msgid ""
"# Green Instantaneous Fraction of Absorbed Photosynthetically Available "
"Radiation (GIFAPAR)\n"
"\n"
"The Green Instantaneous Fraction of Absorbed Photosynthetically Available "
"Radiation (GIFAPAR) is a bio-geophysical product used to study the "
"photosynthetic process of plants and is often used in diagnostic and "
"predictive models computing primary productivity of the vegetation "
"canopies. In addition, this parameter is also an input for the estimation "
"of assimilation of CO2 in vegetation. GIFAPAR ranges from 0–1.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"GreenInstantaneousFractionofAbsorbedPhotosyntheticallyActiveRadiation(GI-"
"FAPAR)S3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-GI-FAPAR)."
msgstr ""
"# Zeleni trenutni delež absorbiranega fotosintetsko razpoložljivega sevanja "
"(GIFAPAR)\n"
"\n"
"Zeleni trenutni delež absorbiranega fotosintetsko razpoložljivega sevanja "
"(GIFAPAR) je biogeofizikalni izdelek, ki se uporablja za preučevanje "
"procesa fotosinteze rastlin in se pogosto uporablja v diagnostičnih in "
"napovednih modelih za izračun primarne produktivnosti vegetacijskih "
"krošenj. Poleg tega je ta parameter tudi vhodni podatek za oceno "
"asimilacije CO2 v vegetaciji. GIFAPAR je v razponu od 0 do 1.\n"
"\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"GreenInstantaneousFractionofAbsorbedPhotosyntheticallyActiveRadiation(GI-"
"FAPAR)S3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-GI-FAPAR)."

msgid ""
"# True Color\n"
"\n"
"This True color script uses the visible light bands red, green and blue in "
"the corresponding red, green and blue color channels, resulting in a "
"natural colored product, that is a good representation of the Earth as "
"humans would see it naturally. For Sentinel-2 L2A Quarterly Cloudless "
"Mosaic, contrast enhancement with highlight compression and saturation "
"enhancement were applied for better visualisation.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel2-quarterly-"
"cloudless-mosaic/true-color/)."
msgstr ""
"# Prave barve\n"
"\n"
"Ta skripta v pravih barvah uporablja kanale vidne svetlobe, rdečega, "
"zelenega in modrega, v ustreznih rdečem, zelenem in modrem barvnem kanalu, "
"kar daje naravno obarvan izdelek, ki dobro predstavlja Zemljo, kot bi jo "
"ljudje videli naravno. Za Sentinel-2 L2A Quarterly Cloudless Mosaic sta "
"bila za boljši prikaz uporabljena izboljšanje kontrasta s stiskanjem "
"svetlih delov in izboljšanje nasičenosti.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel2-quarterly-"
"cloudless-mosaic/true-color/)."

msgid ""
"# False Color\n"
"\n"
"A false color composite uses at least one non-visible wavelength to image "
"Earth. The false color composite using near infrared, red and green bands "
"is very popular (a band is a region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a "
"satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). The false color "
"composite is most commonly used to assess plant density and health, since "
"plants reflect near infrared and green light, while they absorb red. Cities "
"and exposed ground are grey or tan, and water appears blue or black. For "
"Sentinel-2 L2A Quarterly Cloudless Mosaic, the HighlightCompressVisualizer "
"is applied for better visualisation.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel2-quarterly-"
"cloudless-mosaic/false-color/)."
msgstr ""
"# Lažne barve\n"
"\n"
"Kompozit v lažnih barvah za snemanje Zemlje uporablja vsaj eno nevidno "
"valovno dolžino. Zelo priljubljen je kompozit v lažnih barvah z bližnjim "
"infrardečim, rdečim in zelenim kanalom (kanal je območje elektromagnetnega "
"spektra; satelitski senzor lahko Zemljo posname v različnih kanalih). "
"Kompozit v lažnih barvah se najpogosteje uporablja za oceno gostote in "
"zdravja rastlin, saj rastline odbijajo bližnjo infrardečo in zeleno "
"svetlobo, rdečo pa vpijajo. Mesta in izpostavljena tla so siva ali "
"rjavkasta, voda pa je videti modra ali črna. Za Sentinel-2 L2A Quarterly "
"Cloudless Mosaic je za boljši prikaz uporabljen "
"HighlightCompressVisualizer.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel2-quarterly-"
"cloudless-mosaic/false-color/)."

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference vegetation index is a simple, but effective index "
"for quantifying green vegetation. It is a measure of the state of "
"vegetation health based on how plants reflect light at certain wavelengths. "
"The value range of the NDVI is -1 to 1. Negative values of NDVI (values "
"approaching -1) correspond to water. Values close to zero (-0.1 to 0.1) "
"generally correspond to barren areas of rock, sand, or snow. Low, positive "
"values represent shrub and grassland (approximately 0.2 to 0.4), while high "
"values indicate temperate and tropical rainforests (values approaching 1). "
"For Sentinel-2, the NDVI is calculated using NIR band B08 and red band B04: "
"NDVI = (B08 - B04) / (B08 + B04).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel2-quarterly-"
"cloudless-mosaic/ndvi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normaliziran diferenčni vegetacijski indeks (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"Normaliziran diferenčni vegetacijski indeks je preprost, a učinkovit indeks "
"za kvantifikacijo zelene vegetacije. Je merilo zdravstvenega stanja "
"vegetacije, ki temelji na tem, kako rastline odbijajo svetlobo pri "
"določenih valovnih dolžinah. Razpon vrednosti NDVI je od -1 do 1. Negativne "
"vrednosti NDVI (vrednosti, ki se bližajo -1) ustrezajo vodi. Vrednosti "
"blizu nič (od -0,1 do 0,1) običajno ustrezajo nerodovitnim območjem skal, "
"peska ali snega. Nizke pozitivne vrednosti predstavljajo grmičevje in "
"travinje (približno od 0,2 do 0,4), visoke vrednosti pa kažejo na zmerne in "
"tropske deževne gozdove (vrednosti, ki se bližajo 1). Za Sentinel-2 se NDVI "
"izračuna s kanalom NIR B08 in rdečim kanalom B04: NDVI = (B08 - B04) / (B08 "
"+ B04).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel2-quarterly-"
"cloudless-mosaic/ndvi/)."

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Water Index (NDWI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference water index is most appropriate for water body "
"mapping. It uses green and near infrared bands to highlight water bodies, "
"as water strongly absorbs light in the visible to infrared spectrum. Values "
"of water bodies are larger than 0.5. Vegetation has smaller values. "
"Built-up features have positive values between zero and 0.2. The index is "
"sensitive to built-up land and can result in over-estimation of water "
"bodies. For Sentinel-2, the NDWI is calculated using green band B03 and NIR "
"band B08: NDWI = (B03 - B08) / (B03 + B08).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel2-quarterly-"
"cloudless-mosaic/ndwi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normaliziran diferenčni vodni indeks (NDWI)\n"
"\n"
"Normaliziran diferenčni vodni indeks je najprimernejši za kartiranje vodnih "
"teles. Za poudarjanje vodnih teles uporablja zeleni in bližnji infrardeči "
"kanal, saj voda močno vpija svetlobo od vidnega do infrardečega dela "
"spektra. Vrednosti vodnih teles so večje od 0,5. Vegetacija ima manjše "
"vrednosti. Pozidani elementi imajo pozitivne vrednosti med nič in 0,2. "
"Indeks je občutljiv na pozidana zemljišča, zato lahko povzroči preveliko "
"oceno vodnih teles. Za Sentinel-2 se NDWI izračuna z zelenim kanalom B03 in "
"kanalom NIR B08: NDWI = (B03 - B08) / (B03 + B08).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel2-quarterly-"
"cloudless-mosaic/ndwi/)."

msgid ""
"# True Color\n"
"\n"
"This True color script uses the visible light bands red, green and blue in "
"the corresponding red, green and blue color channels, resulting in a "
"natural colored product, that is a good representation of the Earth as "
"humans would see it naturally.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://remotesensing.vito.be/news/simplify-your-processing-"
"worldcover-annual-composites)."
msgstr ""
"# Prave barve\n"
"\n"
"Ta skripta v pravih barvah uporablja kanale vidne svetlobe, rdečega, "
"zelenega in modrega, v ustreznih rdečem, zelenem in modrem barvnem kanalu, "
"kar daje naravno obarvan izdelek, ki dobro predstavlja Zemljo, kot bi jo "
