#, javascript-format
msgid ""
"The **WorldCover Annual Cloudless Mosaics** product offers an almost "
"cloud-free image over the entire globe, created by stitching together the "
"cloudless Sentinel-2 images acquired over a one-year period at a spatial "
"resolution of 10 meters.\n"
"\n"
"More information can be found "
"[here](https://documentation.dataspace.copernicus.eu/Data/SentinelMissions/"
"Sentinel2.html#sentinel-2-level-2a-worldcover-annual-cloudless-mosaic-"
"rgbnir).\n"
"\n"
"**Coverage:** Global Coverage.\n"
"\n"
"**Data availability:** ${ displayRange }\n"
"\n"
"Data for each year is available in the catalog on the 1.1. of the "
"corresponding year.\n"
"\n"
"**Spatial Resolution:** 10 meters.\n"
"\n"
"**Common usage:** Creating Basemaps, Land cover classification, "
"Infrastructure/Land use planning, Environmental monitoring, Water resource "
"management and more."
msgstr ""
"Izdelek **WorldCover Annual Cloudless Mosaics** ponuja skoraj brezoblačen "
"posnetek celotnega sveta, ustvarjen s spajanjem brezoblačnih posnetkov "
"Sentinel-2, zajetih v enoletnem obdobju, s prostorsko ločljivostjo 10 "
"metrov.\n"
"\n"
"Več informacij je na voljo "
"[tukaj](https://documentation.dataspace.copernicus.eu/Data/SentinelMissions/"
"Sentinel2.html#sentinel-2-level-2a-worldcover-annual-cloudless-mosaic-"
"rgbnir).\n"
"\n"
"**Pokritost:** Globalna pokritost.\n"
"\n"
"**Razpoložljivost podatkov:** ${ displayRange }\n"
"\n"
"Podatki za posamezno leto so v katalogu na voljo 1.1. ustreznega leta.\n"
"\n"
"**Prostorska ločljivost:** 10 metrov.\n"
"\n"
"**Običajna uporaba:** Izdelava podlag za karte, klasifikacija pokrovnosti "
"tal, načrtovanje infrastrukture/rabe tal, spremljanje okolja, upravljanje "
"vodnih virov in drugo."

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Water Index (NDWI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference water index is most appropriate for water body "
"mapping. It uses green and near infrared bands to highlight water bodies, "
"as water strongly absorbs light in the visible to infrared spectrum. Values "
"of water bodies are larger than 0.5. Vegetation has smaller values. "
"Built-up features have positive values between zero and 0.2. The index is "
"sensitive to built-up land and can result in over-estimation of water "
"bodies. For Sentinel-2, the NDWI is calculated using green band B03 and NIR "
"band B08: NDWI = (B03 - B08) / (B03 + B08).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://remotesensing.vito.be/news/simplify-your-processing-"
"worldcover-annual-composites)."
msgstr ""
"# Normaliziran diferenčni vodni indeks (NDWI)\n"
"\n"
"Normaliziran diferenčni vodni indeks je najprimernejši za kartiranje vodnih "
"teles. Za poudarjanje vodnih teles uporablja zeleni in bližnji infrardeči "
"kanal, saj voda močno vpija svetlobo od vidnega do infrardečega dela "
"spektra. Vrednosti vodnih teles so večje od 0,5. Vegetacija ima manjše "
"vrednosti. Pozidani elementi imajo pozitivne vrednosti med nič in 0,2. "
"Indeks je občutljiv na pozidana zemljišča, zato lahko povzroči preveliko "
"oceno vodnih teles. Za Sentinel-2 se NDWI izračuna z zelenim kanalom B03 in "
"kanalom NIR B08: NDWI = (B03 - B08) / (B03 + B08).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://remotesensing.vito.be/news/simplify-your-processing-"
"worldcover-annual-composites)."

msgid ""
"# RGB (B17, B05, B02)\n"
"\n"
"This false color composite maps Sentinel-3 OLCI bands B17 (865 nm, "
"near-infrared), B05 (510 nm, cyan-green), and B02 (412.5 nm, violet) into "
"the red, green, and blue display channels respectively. B17 is a "
"near-infrared band used for aerosol and atmospheric correction; placing it "
"in the red channel makes vegetation and land surfaces appear bright red "
"while water remains dark. B05 is sensitive to chlorophyll, sediment, "
"turbidity, and red tide, and B02 captures yellow dissolved organic matter "
"(CDOM) and detrital pigments. The composite is useful for ocean colour "
"analysis, coastal water quality monitoring, and distinguishing turbid or "
"sediment-laden waters from clear ocean.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."
msgstr ""
"# RGB (B17, B05, B02)\n"
"\n"
"Ta kompozit v lažnih barvah preslika kanale Sentinel-3 OLCI B17 (865 nm, "
"bližnji infrardeči), B05 (510 nm, cian-zeleni) in B02 (412,5 nm, vijoličen) "
"v rdeči, zeleni in modri prikazovalni kanal. B17 je bližnji infrardeči "
"kanal, ki se uporablja za popravek aerosolov in atmosfere; ker je v rdečem "
"kanalu, sta vegetacija in kopenska površja videti svetlo rdeča, voda pa "
"ostane temna. B05 je občutljiv na klorofil, sediment, kalnost in rdečo "
"plimo, B02 pa zajema rumeno raztopljeno organsko snov (CDOM) in detritne "
"pigmente. Kompozit je uporaben za analizo barve oceanov, spremljanje "
"kakovosti obalnih voda ter razlikovanje kalnih ali s sedimentom "
"obremenjenih voda od čistega oceana.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."

msgid ""
"# RGB (B17, B06, B03)\n"
"\n"
"This false color composite maps Sentinel-3 OLCI bands B17 (865 nm, "
"near-infrared), B06 (560 nm, green), and B03 (442.5 nm, blue) into the red, "
"green, and blue display channels respectively. B17 is a near-infrared band "
"used for aerosol and atmospheric correction; placing it in the red channel "
"makes vegetation and land surfaces appear bright red while water remains "
"dark. B06 is the chlorophyll absorption minimum reference band, and B03 "
"captures chlorophyll absorption and biogeochemical properties. Compared to "
"the B17/B05/B02 composite, the shifted green and blue channels offer a "
"different sensitivity to phytoplankton and dissolved organic matter in "
"coastal and open ocean waters.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."
msgstr ""
"# RGB (B17, B06, B03)\n"
"\n"
"Ta kompozit v lažnih barvah preslika kanale Sentinel-3 OLCI B17 (865 nm, "
"bližnji infrardeči), B06 (560 nm, zeleni) in B03 (442,5 nm, modri) v rdeči, "
"zeleni in modri prikazovalni kanal. B17 je bližnji infrardeči kanal, ki se "
"uporablja za popravek aerosolov in atmosfere; ker je v rdečem kanalu, sta "
"vegetacija in kopenska površja videti svetlo rdeča, voda pa ostane temna. "
"B06 je referenčni kanal minimuma absorpcije klorofila, B03 pa zajema "
"absorpcijo klorofila in biogeokemijske lastnosti. V primerjavi s kompozitom "
"B17/B05/B02 premaknjena zeleni in modri kanal ponujata drugačno "
"občutljivost na fitoplankton in raztopljeno organsko snov v obalnih in "
"odprtih oceanskih vodah.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."

msgid ""
"The uploaded geometry is invalid (e.g. an unclosed ring, too few points, or "
"duplicate/degenerate vertices). Please fix it and try again."
msgstr ""
"Naložena geometrija je neveljavna (npr. nezaprt obroč, premalo točk ali "
"podvojena/degenerirana oglišča). Popravite jo in poskusite znova."

msgid ""
"The uploaded polygon is not closed: its first and last points differ. Close "
"the ring and try again."
msgstr ""
"Naloženi poligon ni zaprt: njegova prva in zadnja točka se razlikujeta. "
"Zaprite obroč in poskusite znova."

msgid ""
"The uploaded polygon has too few points to form an area. A ring needs at "
"least 3 distinct points. Please fix it and try again."
msgstr ""
"Naloženi poligon ima premalo točk za oblikovanje površine. Obroč potrebuje "
"vsaj 3 različne točke. Popravite ga in poskusite znova."

msgid ""
"The uploaded polygon contains a repeated point (duplicate consecutive "
"vertices). Remove the duplicate point(s) and try again."
msgstr ""
"Naloženi poligon vsebuje ponovljeno točko (podvojena zaporedna oglišča). "
"Odstranite podvojene točke in poskusite znova."

msgid ""
"# SAR False Color Visualization\n"
"\n"
"This script combines the gamma0 of the VV and VH polarizations of "
"Sentinel-1 SAR data into a false color visualization. Water areas appear in "
"blue (partially black) and land in different shades of yellow/green. Urban "
"areas are displayed in light green-yellow (towards white), vegetated areas "
"in mustard green, and bare ground in darker green. The visualization "
"supports a wide range of monitoring applications, including ice and ship "
"tracking, agriculture and deforestation monitoring, and emergency response "
"scenarios such as flood and volcano observation.\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from light green-yellow "
"over brighter green to dark brown or even black. Some general knowledge of "
"the location is helpful to avoid confusing cryogenic features with other "
"land cover types.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_false_color_"
"visualization/)."
msgstr ""
"# Vizualizacija SAR v lažnih barvah\n"
"\n"
"Ta skripta združuje gamma0 polarizacij VV in VH podatkov SAR Sentinel-1 v "
"vizualizacijo v lažnih barvah. Vodna območja so prikazana modro (deloma "
"črno), kopno pa v različnih odtenkih rumene/zelene. Urbana območja so "
"prikazana svetlo zeleno-rumeno (proti beli), vegetacijska območja gorčično "
"zeleno, gola tla pa temneje zeleno. Vizualizacija podpira široko paleto "
"aplikacij spremljanja, vključno s sledenjem ledu in ladij, spremljanjem "
"kmetijstva in krčenja gozdov ter scenariji nujnega odzivanja, kot sta "
"opazovanje poplav in vulkanov.\n"
"\n"
"Za zasnežena in poledenela območja se vizualizacija lahko spreminja od "
"svetlo zeleno-rumene prek svetlejše zelene do temno rjave ali celo črne. "
"Nekaj splošnega poznavanja lokacije je koristno, da kriogenih značilnosti "
"ne zamenjate z drugimi vrstami pokrovnosti tal.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_false_color_"
"visualization/)."

msgid ""
"# Urban Areas\n"
"\n"
"This script uses Sentinel-1 SAR VH and VV polarisations to highlight urban "
"areas and buildings. Structures appear in different colours depending on "
"their backscatter characteristics: purple indicates high VH reflectance, "
"green indicates high VV reflectance, and white indicates high reflectance "
"in both. The red channel is restricted to pixels where VH exceeds 0.5, "
"helping separate buildings from bare soil. The script is useful for "
"monitoring urban expansion, assessing building density, and identifying "
"structures in flood-prone areas. Note that in mountainous terrain, steep "
"slopes and snow can produce similar signals, making it difficult to "
"separate urban areas from other features.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."
msgstr ""
"# Urbana območja\n"
"\n"
"Ta skripta uporablja polarizaciji VH in VV SAR Sentinel-1 za poudarjanje "
"urbanih območij in stavb. Strukture so glede na značilnosti povratnega "
"sipanja prikazane v različnih barvah: vijolična kaže visoko odbojnost VH, "
"zelena visoko odbojnost VV, bela pa visoko odbojnost v obeh. Rdeči kanal je "
"omejen na piksle, kjer VH presega 0,5, kar pomaga ločiti stavbe od golih "
"tal. Skripta je uporabna za spremljanje širjenja mest, ocenjevanje gostote "
"pozidave in prepoznavanje struktur na poplavno ogroženih območjih. "
"Upoštevajte, da lahko v gorskem terenu strma pobočja in sneg dajejo podobne "
"signale, zaradi česar je težko ločiti urbana območja od drugih značilnosti.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."

msgid ""
"# SAR Deforestation Detection\n"
"\n"
"This script processes Sentinel-1 VV and VH polarisation bands to detect "
"deforestation and forest degradation. It converts the backscatter values "
"into polar form to derive vector length and angle, which discriminate "
"between water, forest, and bare soil. Water and bare soil appear black, "
"forested areas are rendered in green gradients, and degraded or cleared "
"areas appear in red — with stronger colours indicating higher "
"classification confidence. The script is useful for monitoring forest loss "
"and land-use change over time.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_deforestation_"
"detection/)."
msgstr ""
"# Zaznavanje krčenja gozdov s SAR\n"
"\n"
"Ta skripta obdeluje kanala polarizacij VV in VH Sentinel-1 za zaznavanje "
"krčenja in degradacije gozdov. Vrednosti povratnega sipanja pretvori v "
"polarno obliko, da izpelje dolžino in kot vektorja, ki razlikujeta med "
"vodo, gozdom in golimi tlemi. Voda in gola tla so črna, gozdnata območja so "
"prikazana v zelenih gradientih, degradirana ali izkrčena območja pa rdeče – "
"močnejše barve kažejo višjo zanesljivost klasifikacije. Skripta je uporabna "
"za spremljanje izgube gozdov in sprememb rabe tal skozi čas.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_"
"deforestation_detection/)."

msgid ""
"# Water Surface Roughness\n"
"\n"
"This script visualizes water surface roughness using Sentinel-1 SAR data. "
"SAR backscatter is highly sensitive to the roughness of the water surface: "
"calm water reflects radar energy away from the sensor and appears dark, "
"while rough or wind-driven water scatters energy back and appears brighter. "
"Variations in surface roughness reveal oceanographic and maritime features "
"such as wind patterns, sea currents, internal waves, and ship wakes. Oil "
"spills dampen surface waves and appear as dark patches against the "
"surrounding rougher water. The visualization supports maritime monitoring "
"applications including ship tracking, oil pollution detection, and "
"observation of ocean circulation.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/water_surface_"
"roughness_visualization/)."
msgstr ""
"# Hrapavost vodne površine\n"
"\n"
"Ta skripta vizualizira hrapavost vodne površine s podatki SAR Sentinel-1. "
"Povratno sipanje SAR je zelo občutljivo na hrapavost vodne površine: mirna "
"voda odbija radarsko energijo stran od senzorja in je videti temna, "
"razburkana ali z vetrom gnana voda pa energijo sipa nazaj in je videti "
"svetlejša. Razlike v hrapavosti površine razkrivajo oceanografske in "
"pomorske značilnosti, kot so vzorci vetra, morski tokovi, notranji valovi "
"in sledi ladij. Razlitja nafte dušijo površinske valove in so videti kot "
"temne lise na okoliški bolj hrapavi vodi. Vizualizacija podpira aplikacije "
"pomorskega spremljanja, vključno s sledenjem ladij, zaznavanjem onesnaženja "
"z nafto in opazovanjem oceanskega kroženja.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/water_surface_"
"roughness_visualization/)."

msgid ""
"Water and ice cover classification from Sentinel-1 imagery within water "
"bodies defined by the input water mask. Classes include open water (1), "
"snow-covered or snow-free ice (100), radar limitations such as shadow, "
"layover, or foreshortening (200), and no data (255)."
msgstr ""
"Klasifikacija vodne in ledene odeje iz posnetkov Sentinel-1 znotraj vodnih "
"teles, določenih z vhodno vodno masko. Razredi vključujejo odprto vodo (1), "
"z ali brez snega prekrit led (100), radarske omejitve, kot so senca, "
"prekrivanje ali skrajšanje (200), in ni podatkov (255)."

msgid "Quality layer providing basic assessment of the Water/Ice Cover layer."
msgstr "Sloj kakovosti, ki zagotavlja osnovno oceno sloja vodne/ledene odeje."

msgid ""
"The default visualisation highlights inland water surfaces over which the "
"water/ice classification is performed; these correspond to pixels where bit "
"15 is activated. Additional information can also be visualised by selecting "
"other bits. More details are available in the </> Custom option."
msgstr ""
"Privzeti prikaz poudari celinske vodne površine, nad katerimi se izvaja "
"klasifikacija vode/ledu; ti ustrezajo pikslom, kjer je aktiviran bit 15. Z "
"izbiro drugih bitov je mogoče prikazati tudi dodatne informacije. Več "
"podrobnosti je na voljo v možnosti </> Po meri."

msgid "WIC S1 Europe 60m Daily V1"
msgstr "WIC S1 Europe 60m Daily V1"

msgid "CPMCH 10m Yearly (2017–present)"
msgstr "CPMCH 10m Yearly (2017–present)"

msgid "CPMCE 10m Yearly (2017–present)"
msgstr "CPMCE 10m Yearly (2017–present)"

msgid ""
"The High Resolution Layer Cropping Patterns - Main Crop Harvest (CPMCH) "
"raster product provides the harvest date of the main (annual) crop "
"expressed in days of the year (DOY). The harvest is considered as the time "
"of removal of most of the biomass. YYDOY where YY = last 2 digits of the "
"year (e.g. 19 for 2019) and DOY is the day of the year (1-365).\n"
"\n"
"This dataset is provided annually starting in 2017 with 10 meter rasters "
"(fully conformant with the EEA reference grid) in 100 x 100 km tiles "
"covering the EEA38 countries.\n"
"\n"
"High Resolution Layer Croplands product is part of the European Union's "
"Copernicus Land Monitoring Service. Confidence layer available for the "
"dataset.\n"
"\n"
"This dataset includes data from the French Overseas Territories (DOMs). "
"More information "
"[here](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/high-resolution-layer-"
"croplands)."
msgstr ""
"Rastrski izdelek High Resolution Layer Cropping Patterns - Main Crop "
"Harvest (CPMCH) zagotavlja datum žetve glavnega (enoletnega) posevka, "
"izražen v dnevih v letu (DOY). Za žetev velja čas odstranitve večine "
"biomase. YYDOY, kjer je YY = zadnji dve števki leta (npr. 19 za 2019), DOY "
"pa je dan v letu (1-365).\n"
"\n"
"Ta zbirka podatkov je na voljo letno od leta 2017 naprej v rastrih "
"ločljivosti 10 metrov (popolnoma skladnih z referenčno mrežo EEA) v "
"ploščicah 100 x 100 km, ki pokrivajo države EEA38.\n"
"\n"
"Izdelek High Resolution Layer Croplands je del storitve Copernicus za "
"spremljanje kopenskega površja Evropske unije. Za zbirko podatkov je na "
"voljo sloj zaupanja.\n"
"\n"
"Ta zbirka podatkov vključuje podatke francoskih čezmorskih ozemelj (DOM). "
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/high-resolution-layer-"
"croplands)."

msgid ""
"Extent of open-water and ice across the continent derived from Sentinel-2 "
"optical imagery. A water mask is applied to distinguish snow on ice-covered "
"water bodies from snow on land. The primary classes are open water (1), "
"snow-covered or snow-free ice (100), and other features (254), which "
"include land, vegetation, salt seas, and other surface types. The dataset "
"has also the following classes for areas where water/ice classification "
"cannot be determined from Sentinel-2 optical imagery: cloud or cloud shadow "
"(205), and no data (255)."
msgstr ""
"Obseg odprte vode in ledu na celini, izpeljan iz optičnih posnetkov "
"Sentinel-2. Za razlikovanje snega na z ledom prekritih vodnih telesih od "
"snega na kopnem se uporablja vodna maska. Glavni razredi so odprta voda "
"(1), z ali brez snega prekrit led (100) in druge značilnosti (254), ki "
"vključujejo kopno, vegetacijo, slana morja in druge vrste površja. Zbirka "
"podatkov ima tudi naslednje razrede za območja, kjer klasifikacije "
"vode/ledu ni mogoče določiti iz optičnih posnetkov Sentinel-2: oblak ali "
"senca oblaka (205) in ni podatkov (255)."

msgid ""
"The default visualisation indicates whether a pixel is located in the "
"hillshade; these correspond to pixels where bit 0 is activated. Additional "
"information can also be visualised by selecting other bits. More details "
"are available in the </> Custom option."
msgstr ""
"Privzeti prikaz kaže, ali je piksel v reliefni senci; ti ustrezajo pikslom, "
"kjer je aktiviran bit 0. Z izbiro drugih bitov je mogoče prikazati tudi "
"dodatne informacije. Več podrobnosti je na voljo v možnosti </> Po meri."

msgid ""
"Confidence level of the Random Forest classifier for the class assigned in "
"the WIC layer (0-100%)."
msgstr ""
"Stopnja zaupanja klasifikatorja Random Forest za razred, dodeljen v sloju "
"WIC (0-100 %)."

msgid "WIC S2 Europe 20m Daily V1"
msgstr "WIC S2 Europe 20m Daily V1"

msgid ""
"Water and ice cover classification from Sentinel-2 (optical) or Sentinel-1 "
"(radar) imagery within water bodies defined by the input water mask. The "
"primary classes are open water (1), snow-covered or snow-free ice (100), "
"and other features (254), which include land, vegetation, salt seas, and "
"other surface types. When classification is not possible, specific values "
"indicate radar-related limitations (shadow, layover, foreshortening - 200), "
"cloud or cloud shadow in optical images (205), or no data (255)."
msgstr ""
"Klasifikacija vodne in ledene odeje iz posnetkov Sentinel-2 (optični) ali "
"Sentinel-1 (radarski) znotraj vodnih teles, določenih z vhodno vodno masko. "
"Glavni razredi so odprta voda (1), z ali brez snega prekrit led (100) in "
"druge značilnosti (254), ki vključujejo kopno, vegetacijo, slana morja in "
"druge vrste površja. Kadar klasifikacija ni mogoča, posebne vrednosti "
"kažejo radarske omejitve (senca, prekrivanje, skrajšanje - 200), oblak ali "
"senco oblaka v optičnih posnetkih (205) ali ni podatkov (255)."

msgid ""
"Bitmask layer with pixel quality flags. The default visualisation displays "
"the satellite sensor type used for the classification (optical=0 in blue, "
"radar=1 in pink). These correspond to pixels where bit 9 is activated. "
"Additional information can also be visualised by selecting other bits. More "
"details are available in the </> Custom option."
msgstr ""
"Sloj bitne maske z zastavicami kakovosti pikslov. Privzeti prikaz kaže "
"vrsto satelitskega senzorja, uporabljenega za klasifikacijo (optični=0 "
"modro, radarski=1 roza). Ti ustrezajo pikslom, kjer je aktiviran bit 9. Z "
"izbiro drugih bitov je mogoče prikazati tudi dodatne informacije. Več "
"podrobnosti je na voljo v možnosti </> Po meri."

msgid "WIC S1+S2 Europe 20m Daily V1"
msgstr "WIC S1+S2 Europe 20m Daily V1"

#, javascript-format
msgid "Showing ${ processedResults.length } of ${ totalFilteredResults } results"
msgstr ""
"Prikazanih ${ processedResults.length } od ${ totalFilteredResults } "
"rezultatov"

msgid ""
"Bitmask layer with pixel quality flags. The default visualisation displays "
"the sensor type of the satellite data (optical=0 in blue, radar=1 in pink). "
"These correspond to pixels where bit 7 is activated. Additional information "
"can also be visualised by selecting other bits. More details are available "
"in the </> Custom option."
msgstr ""
"Sloj bitne maske z zastavicami kakovosti pikslov. Privzeti prikaz kaže "
"vrsto senzorja satelitskih podatkov (optični=0 modro, radarski=1 roza). Ti "
"ustrezajo pikslom, kjer je aktiviran bit 7. Z izbiro drugih bitov je mogoče "
"prikazati tudi dodatne informacije. Več podrobnosti je na voljo v možnosti "
"</> Po meri."

msgid ""
"Bitmask layer with pixel quality flags. The default visualisation displays "
"the areas where wet snow detection is performed (high elevation, "
"non-forested, non-urban, non-water areas). These correspond to pixels where "
"bit 7 is activated. Additional information can also be visualised by "
"selecting other bits. More details are available in the </> Custom option."
msgstr ""
"Sloj bitne maske z zastavicami kakovosti pikslov. Privzeti prikaz kaže "
"območja, kjer poteka zaznavanje mokrega snega (višje ležeča, negozdnata, "
"neurbana območja brez vode). Ti ustrezajo pikslom, kjer je aktiviran bit 7. "
"Z izbiro drugih bitov je mogoče prikazati tudi dodatne informacije. Več "
"podrobnosti je na voljo v možnosti </> Po meri."

msgid ""
"The Cloud Classification (CC) product provides information on the extent of "
"clouds and cloud shadows derived from optical satellite data acquired by "
"the **Sentinel-2** constellation. Cloud detection is performed at a "
"**120m** spatial resolution using the [MAJA "
"software](https://gitlab.orfeo-toolbox.org/maja/maja/).<br><br>It is "
"generated in near real-time at European scale, with a pixel spacing of 20 m "
"x 20 m. It used to produce the CLMS High-Resolution Water, Snow and Ice "
"datasets (HR-WSI), which rely on Sentinel-2 imagery.<br><br>**Data "
"availability**: from 2016 to the present. No product is generated for a "
"Sentinel-2 tile when cloud cover exceeds 90%.<br><br>More information in "
"the products documentation "
"[here](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/snow/fractional-snow-cover)."
msgstr ""
"Izdelek Cloud Classification (CC) zagotavlja informacije o obsegu oblakov "
"in senc oblakov, izpeljanih iz optičnih satelitskih podatkov konstelacije "
"**Sentinel-2**. Zaznavanje oblakov poteka s prostorsko ločljivostjo **120 "
"m** z uporabo [programske opreme "
"MAJA](https://gitlab.orfeo-toolbox.org/maja/maja/).<br><br>Ustvarja se "
"skoraj v realnem času v evropskem merilu z razmikom pikslov 20 m x 20 m. "
"Uporablja se za izdelavo zbirk podatkov CLMS High-Resolution Water, Snow "
"and Ice (HR-WSI), ki temeljijo na posnetkih "
"Sentinel-2.<br><br>**Razpoložljivost podatkov**: od 2016 do danes. Za "
"ploščico Sentinel-2 se izdelek ne ustvari, kadar oblačnost presega 90 "
"%.<br><br>Več informacij v dokumentaciji izdelkov "
"[tukaj](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/snow/fractional-snow-cover)."

msgid ""
"The **SAR Wet Snow (SWS)** product provides the wet snow extent for high "
"mountain areas, based on C-band Synthetic Aperture Radar satellite data "
"from the **Sentinel-1** constellation.<br><br>It is generated in near "
"real-time for selected high mountain areas at European scale with a spatial "
"resolution of **60 m x 60 m**.<br><br>**Data availability**: from 2016 to "
"the present.<br><br>More information "
"[here](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/snow/high-resolution-sar-wet-"
"snow)."
msgstr ""
"Izdelek **SAR Wet Snow (SWS)** zagotavlja obseg mokrega snega za "
"visokogorska območja na podlagi satelitskih podatkov radarja s sintetično "
"odprtino (SAR) v pasu C konstelacije **Sentinel-1**.<br><br>Ustvarja se "
"skoraj v realnem času za izbrana visokogorska območja v evropskem merilu s "
"prostorsko ločljivostjo **60 m x 60 m**.<br><br>**Razpoložljivost "
"podatkov**: od 2016 do danes.<br><br>Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/snow/high-resolution-sar-wet-"
"snow)."

msgid ""
"The **Wet / Dry Snow (WDS)** product provides information on the snow state "
"(wet or dry) by combining **Sentinel-1** radar-based wet snow maps within "
"the snow cover extent derived from **Sentinel-2** optical data. Cloud "
"detection in the Sentinel-2 imagery is performed using the [MAJA "
"software](https://gitlab.orfeo-toolbox.org/maja/maja/).<br><br>It is "
"generated in near real-time at European scale, with a spatial resolution of "
"**60 m x 60 m** in areas where Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 observation tracks "
"overlap.<br><br>**Data availability**: from 2016 to the present. No product "
"is generated for a Sentinel-2 tile when cloud cover exceeds "
"90%.<br><br>More information "
"[here](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/snow/high-resolution-wet-dry-"
"snow)."
msgstr ""
"Izdelek **Wet / Dry Snow (WDS)** zagotavlja informacije o stanju snega "
"(moker ali suh) z združevanjem radarskih zemljevidov mokrega snega "
"**Sentinel-1** znotraj obsega snežne odeje, izpeljanega iz optičnih "
"podatkov **Sentinel-2**. Zaznavanje oblakov v posnetkih Sentinel-2 poteka z "
"uporabo [programske opreme "
"MAJA](https://gitlab.orfeo-toolbox.org/maja/maja/).<br><br>Ustvarja se "
"skoraj v realnem času v evropskem merilu s prostorsko ločljivostjo **60 m x "
"60 m** na območjih, kjer se sledi opazovanja Sentinel-1 in Sentinel-2 "
"prekrivajo.<br><br>**Razpoložljivost podatkov**: od 2016 do danes. Za "
"ploščico Sentinel-2 se izdelek ne ustvari, kadar oblačnost presega 90 "
"%.<br><br>Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/snow/high-resolution-wet-dry-"
"snow)."

msgid ""
"The Sentinel-1 & Sentinel-2 **Snow Phenology (SP S1+S2)** product "
"characterizes the timing and duration of the snow season. For each pixel "
"and for a given hydrological year, it provides the number of days with snow "
"cover, as well as the first and last day of the longest continuous snow "
"period. The hydrological year starts on 1 September.<br><br>The product is "
"generated at the European scale with a spatial resolution of **60 m x 60 "
"m**, consistent with the input snow cover maps derived from optical "
"satellite data acquired by the Sentinel-2 constellation and from C-band "
"Synthetic Aperture Radar satellite data acquired by the Sentinel-1 "
"constellation (Gap-filled Fractional Snow Cover - GFSC).<br><br>**Data "
"availability**: from 2016 to the present. The data can be downloaded in "
"multiple projections and pixel spacings.<br><br>More information "
"[here](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/snow/high-resolution-snow-"
"phenology)."
msgstr ""
"Izdelek Sentinel-1 & Sentinel-2 **Snow Phenology (SP S1+S2)** opisuje čas "
"in trajanje snežne sezone. Za vsak piksel in dano hidrološko leto "
"zagotavlja število dni s snežno odejo ter prvi in zadnji dan najdaljšega "
"neprekinjenega snežnega obdobja. Hidrološko leto se začne 1. "
"septembra.<br><br>Izdelek se ustvarja v evropskem merilu s prostorsko "
"ločljivostjo **60 m x 60 m**, skladno z vhodnimi zemljevidi snežne odeje, "
"izpeljanimi iz optičnih satelitskih podatkov konstelacije Sentinel-2 in iz "
"satelitskih podatkov radarja s sintetično odprtino v pasu C konstelacije "
"Sentinel-1 (Gap-filled Fractional Snow Cover - "
"GFSC).<br><br>**Razpoložljivost podatkov**: od 2016 do danes. Podatke je "
"mogoče prenesti v več projekcijah in z več razmiki pikslov.<br><br>Več "
"informacij "
"[tukaj](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/snow/high-resolution-snow-"
"phenology)."

msgid ""
"The **Water Cover Duration (WCD)** product estimates the number of days "
"land is covered by water. For each pixel and for a given hydrological year, "
"it indicates how frequently water is present. The hydrological year starts "
"on 1 September. It is based on water masks derived from **Sentinel-1** "
"radar and **Sentinel-2** optical data, combined with Water/Ice Cover data "
"from Sentinel-2 (WIC S2).<br><br>The product is generated at the European "
"scale with a spatial resolution of **10 m x 10 m**.<br><br>**Data "
"availability**: from 2016 to the present. The data can be downloaded in "
"multiple projections and pixel spacings.<br><br>More information "
"[here](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/water-bodies/high-resolution-"
"water-cover-duration)."
msgstr ""
"Izdelek **Water Cover Duration (WCD)** ocenjuje število dni, ko je kopno "
"prekrito z vodo. Za vsak piksel in dano hidrološko leto kaže, kako pogosto "
"je voda prisotna. Hidrološko leto se začne 1. septembra. Temelji na vodnih "
"maskah, izpeljanih iz radarskih podatkov **Sentinel-1** in optičnih "
"podatkov **Sentinel-2**, v kombinaciji s podatki Water/Ice Cover iz "
"Sentinel-2 (WIC S2).<br><br>Izdelek se ustvarja v evropskem merilu s "
"prostorsko ločljivostjo **10 m x 10 m**.<br><br>**Razpoložljivost "
"podatkov**: od 2016 do danes. Podatke je mogoče prenesti v več projekcijah "
"in z več razmiki pikslov.<br><br>Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/water-bodies/high-resolution-"
"water-cover-duration)."

msgid ""
"The **Ice Cover Duration (ICD)** product describes how long inland waters "
"are covered by ice. For each pixel and for a given hydrological year, it "
"provides the number of days with ice cover. The hydrological year starts on "
"1 September. It is based on ice cover maps derived from **Sentinel-2** "
"optical data (Water/Ice Cover WIC S2) and **Sentinel-1** C-band Synthetic "
"Aperture Radar data (Water/Ice Cover WIC S1).<br><br>The product is "
"generated at the European scale with a spatial resolution of **20 m x 20 "
"m**.<br><br>**Data availability**: from 2016 to the present. The data can "
"be downloaded in multiple projections and pixel spacings.<br><br>More "
"information "
"[here](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/water-bodies/high-resolution-"
"ice-cover-duration)."
msgstr ""
"Izdelek **Ice Cover Duration (ICD)** opisuje, kako dolgo so celinske vode "
"prekrite z ledom. Za vsak piksel in dano hidrološko leto zagotavlja število "
"dni z ledeno odejo. Hidrološko leto se začne 1. septembra. Temelji na "
"zemljevidih ledene odeje, izpeljanih iz optičnih podatkov **Sentinel-2** "
"(Water/Ice Cover WIC S2) in podatkov radarja s sintetično odprtino v pasu C "
"**Sentinel-1** (Water/Ice Cover WIC S1).<br><br>Izdelek se ustvarja v "
"evropskem merilu s prostorsko ločljivostjo **20 m x 20 "
"m**.<br><br>**Razpoložljivost podatkov**: od 2016 do danes. Podatke je "
"mogoče prenesti v več projekcijah in z več razmiki pikslov.<br><br>Več "
"informacij "
"[tukaj](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/water-bodies/high-resolution-"
"ice-cover-duration)."

msgid ""
"The **Water and Ice Cover by Sentinel-1 (WICS1)** product provides "
"information about river and lake areas covered by snow-covered or snow-free "
"ice. It is based on synthetic aperture radar data from the **Sentinel-1** "
"constellation.<br><br>It is generated in near real-time at European scale, "
"with a spatial resolution of **60 m x 60 m**.<br><br>**Data availability**: "
"from 2016 to the present.<br><br>More information "
"[here](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/water-bodies/water-and-ice-"
"cover-raster-20-m-60-m-europe-daily)."
msgstr ""
"Izdelek **Water and Ice Cover by Sentinel-1 (WICS1)** zagotavlja "
"informacije o območjih rek in jezer, prekritih z ledom, z ali brez snega. "
"Temelji na podatkih radarja s sintetično odprtino konstelacije "
"**Sentinel-1**.<br><br>Ustvarja se skoraj v realnem času v evropskem merilu "
"s prostorsko ločljivostjo **60 m x 60 m**.<br><br>**Razpoložljivost "
"podatkov**: od 2016 do danes.<br><br>Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/water-bodies/water-and-ice-"
"cover-raster-20-m-60-m-europe-daily)."

msgid ""
"The **Water and Ice Cover by Sentinel-2 (WICS2)** product provides the "
"water and ice extent over land. A water mask is used to differentiate "
"between snow on ice-covered water areas and snow on land. Cloud detection "
"in the Sentinel-2 imagery is performed using the [MAJA "
"software](https://gitlab.orfeo-toolbox.org/maja/maja/).<br><br>It is "
"generated in near real-time at European scale based on optical satellite "
"data from the Sentinel-2 constellation, with a spatial resolution of **20 m "
"x 20 m**.<br><br>**Data availability**: from 2016 to the present. No "
"product is generated for a Sentinel-2 tile when cloud cover exceeds "
"90%.<br><br>More information "
"[here](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/water-bodies/water-and-ice-"
"cover-raster-20-m-60-m-europe-daily)."
msgstr ""
"Izdelek **Water and Ice Cover by Sentinel-2 (WICS2)** zagotavlja obseg vode "
"in ledu nad kopnim. Vodna maska se uporablja za razlikovanje med snegom na "
"z ledom prekritih vodnih območjih in snegom na kopnem. Zaznavanje oblakov v "
"posnetkih Sentinel-2 poteka z uporabo [programske opreme "
"MAJA](https://gitlab.orfeo-toolbox.org/maja/maja/).<br><br>Ustvarja se "
"skoraj v realnem času v evropskem merilu na podlagi optičnih satelitskih "
"podatkov konstelacije Sentinel-2 s prostorsko ločljivostjo **20 m x 20 "
"m**.<br><br>**Razpoložljivost podatkov**: od 2016 do danes. Za ploščico "
"Sentinel-2 se izdelek ne ustvari, kadar oblačnost presega 90 %.<br><br>Več "
"informacij "
"[tukaj](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/water-bodies/water-and-ice-"
"cover-raster-20-m-60-m-europe-daily)."

msgid ""
"The **Fractional Snow Cover (FSC)** product provides the fraction of the "
"surface covered by snow at the top of canopy (FSC-TOC) and on ground "
"(FSC-OG) per pixel as a percentage (0% – 100%). Cloud detection in the "
"Sentinel-2 imagery is performed using the [MAJA "
"software](https://gitlab.orfeo-toolbox.org/maja/maja/).<br><br>It is "
"generated in near real-time at European scale based on optical satellite "
"data from the **Sentinel-2** constellation, with a spatial resolution of "
"**20 m x 20 m**.<br><br>**Data availability**: from 2016 to the present. No "
"product is generated for a Sentinel-2 tile when cloud cover exceeds "
"90%.<br><br>More information "
"[here](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/snow/fractional-snow-cover)."
msgstr ""
"Izdelek **Fractional Snow Cover (FSC)** zagotavlja delež površja, "
"prekritega s snegom, na vrhu krošenj (FSC-TOC) in na tleh (FSC-OG) na "
"piksel v odstotkih (0 % – 100 %). Zaznavanje oblakov v posnetkih Sentinel-2 "
"poteka z uporabo [programske opreme "
"MAJA](https://gitlab.orfeo-toolbox.org/maja/maja/).<br><br>Ustvarja se "
"skoraj v realnem času v evropskem merilu na podlagi optičnih satelitskih "
"podatkov konstelacije **Sentinel-2** s prostorsko ločljivostjo **20 m x 20 "
"m**.<br><br>**Razpoložljivost podatkov**: od 2016 do danes. Za ploščico "
"Sentinel-2 se izdelek ne ustvari, kadar oblačnost presega 90 %.<br><br>Več "
"informacij "
"[tukaj](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/snow/fractional-snow-cover)."

msgid ""
"The daily cumulative **Gap-filled Fractional Snow Cover (GFSC)** product "
"provides pixel-wise snow cover extent as a percentage (0% – 100%). It is "
"based on synthetic aperture radar (SAR) data from the **Sentinel-1** "
"constellation and optical imagery from the **Sentinel-2** constellation. "
"The product is generated by merging all available Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 "
"observations acquired over the previous **seven days** to produce a "
"spatially complete composite of snow conditions, thereby reducing data gaps "
"caused by cloud cover and sensor coverage limitations. Snow information "
"derived from Sentinel-1 is focused on the detection of wet snow in "
"high-mountain areas.<br><br>It is generated on a daily basis at European "
"scale, with a spatial resolution of **60 m x 60 m**.<br><br>**Data "
"availability**: from 2016 to the present.<br><br>More information "
"[here](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/snow/high-resolution-gap-"
"filled-fractional-snow-cover)."
msgstr ""
"Dnevni kumulativni izdelek **Gap-filled Fractional Snow Cover (GFSC)** "
"zagotavlja obseg snežne odeje po pikslih v odstotkih (0 % – 100 %). Temelji "
"na podatkih radarja s sintetično odprtino (SAR) konstelacije **Sentinel-1** "
"in optičnih posnetkih konstelacije **Sentinel-2**. Izdelek nastane z "
"združitvijo vseh razpoložljivih opazovanj Sentinel-1 in Sentinel-2, zajetih "
"v preteklih **sedmih dneh**, da se ustvari prostorsko popoln kompozit "
"snežnih razmer, s čimer se zmanjšajo vrzeli v podatkih zaradi oblačnosti in "
"omejitev pokritosti senzorjev. Informacije o snegu, izpeljane iz "
"Sentinel-1, so osredotočene na zaznavanje mokrega snega v visokogorskih "
"območjih.<br><br>Ustvarja se dnevno v evropskem merilu s prostorsko "
"ločljivostjo **60 m x 60 m**.<br><br>**Razpoložljivost podatkov**: od 2016 "
"do danes.<br><br>Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/snow/high-resolution-gap-"
"filled-fractional-snow-cover)."

msgid ""
"The Sentinel-2 **Snow Phenology (SP S2)** product characterizes the timing "
"and duration of the snow season. For each pixel and for a given "
"hydrological year, it provides the number of days with snow cover, as well "
"as the first and last day of the longest continuous snow period. The "
"hydrological year starts on 1 September.<br><br>The product is generated at "
"the European scale with a spatial resolution of **20 m x 20 m**, consistent "
"with the input snow cover maps derived from optical satellite data acquired "
"by the Sentinel-2 constellation (Fractional Snow Cover - "
"FSC).<br><br>**Data availability**: from 2016 to the present. The data can "
"be downloaded in multiple projections and pixel spacings.<br><br>More "
"information "
"[here](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/snow/high-resolution-snow-"
"phenology)."
msgstr ""
"Izdelek Sentinel-2 **Snow Phenology (SP S2)** opisuje čas in trajanje "
"snežne sezone. Za vsak piksel in dano hidrološko leto zagotavlja število "
"dni s snežno odejo ter prvi in zadnji dan najdaljšega neprekinjenega "
"snežnega obdobja. Hidrološko leto se začne 1. septembra.<br><br>Izdelek se "
"ustvarja v evropskem merilu s prostorsko ločljivostjo **20 m x 20 m**, "
"skladno z vhodnimi zemljevidi snežne odeje, izpeljanimi iz optičnih "
"satelitskih podatkov konstelacije Sentinel-2 (Fractional Snow Cover - "
"FSC).<br><br>**Razpoložljivost podatkov**: od 2016 do danes. Podatke je "
"mogoče prenesti v več projekcijah in z več razmiki pikslov.<br><br>Več "
"informacij "
"[tukaj](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/snow/high-resolution-snow-"
"phenology)."

#. Shared across CLMS collections that expose these structural OData attributes.
msgid ""
"Applies to all sub-categories. The format in which the data is stored "
"(NetCDF or Cloud Optimized GeoTIFF)."
msgstr ""
"Velja za vse podkategorije. Oblika, v kateri so podatki shranjeni (NetCDF "
"ali Cloud Optimized GeoTIFF)."

msgid ""
"Applies to all sub-categories. The unique identifier for the specific "
"dataset within this collection."
msgstr ""
"Velja za vse podkategorije. Enolični identifikator posamezne zbirke "
"podatkov znotraj te zbirke."

msgid ""
"Applies to all sub-categories. The type of product, identifying the "
"thematic category or processing pipeline."
msgstr ""
"Velja za vse podkategorije. Vrsta izdelka, ki določa tematsko kategorijo "
"ali procesni potek."

msgid ""
"Only applies to data sources within the Snow, Water Bodies and Auxiliary "
"Data categories."
msgstr ""
"Velja samo za vire podatkov znotraj kategorij Sneg, Vodna telesa in Pomožni "
"podatki."

msgid ""
"Applies to all sub-categories. Missions whose input data was used to "
"process the product."
msgstr ""
"Velja za vse podkategorije. Misije, katerih vhodni podatki so bili "
"uporabljeni za obdelavo izdelka."

msgid ""
"Near real-time consolidation level (RT0–RT6). RT0 is the fastest delivery; "
"RT6 has the highest accuracy. Only applies to data sources within the "
"Vegetation category."
msgstr ""
"Raven konsolidacije skoraj v realnem času (RT0–RT6). RT0 je najhitrejša "
"dostava; RT6 ima najvišjo natančnost. Velja samo za vire podatkov znotraj "
"kategorije Vegetacija."

msgid ""
"The **Water and Ice Cover by Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 (WIC S1+S2)** "
"product shows which river and lake areas are covered by ice, with or "
"without snow. It combines data from two types of instruments acquired on "
"the same day to increase coverage and reduce missing information. It uses "
"water/ice cover information derived from **Sentinel-2** optical images (WIC "
"S2), and from **Sentinel-1** radar data (WIC S1).<br><br>The product is "
"generated in near real-time at European scale, with a spatial resolution of "
"**20 m x 20 m**.<br><br>**Data availability**: from 2016 to the "
"present.<br><br>More information "
"[here](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/water-bodies/water-and-ice-"
"cover-raster-20-m-60-m-europe-daily)."
msgstr ""
"Izdelek **Water and Ice Cover by Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 (WIC S1+S2)** "
"kaže, katera območja rek in jezer so prekrita z ledom, z ali brez snega. "
"Združuje podatke dveh vrst instrumentov, zajetih isti dan, da poveča "
"pokritost in zmanjša manjkajoče informacije. Uporablja informacije o "
"vodni/ledeni odeji, izpeljane iz optičnih posnetkov **Sentinel-2** (WIC S2) "
"in iz radarskih podatkov **Sentinel-1** (WIC S1).<br><br>Izdelek se "
"ustvarja skoraj v realnem času v evropskem merilu s prostorsko ločljivostjo "
"**20 m x 20 m**.<br><br>**Razpoložljivost podatkov**: od 2016 do "
"danes.<br><br>Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/water-bodies/water-and-ice-"
"cover-raster-20-m-60-m-europe-daily)."

msgid ""
"The mosaicking order controls which data is used where imagery overlaps on "
"the map. Fills overlapping areas with either the newest (most recent) or "
"oldest (least recent) acquisition."
msgstr ""
"Vrstni red mozaičenja določa, kateri podatki se uporabijo tam, kjer se "
"posnetki na karti prekrivajo. Prekrivajoča se območja zapolni z najnovejšim "
"(najnovejši) ali najstarejšim (najstarejši) zajemom."

msgid ""
"No products were found for the selected search parameters.\n"
"\n"
"The filters you've applied might be limiting your results. To get more "
"results, try selecting more data sources, extending the time range or "
"selecting a larger area on the map. You could also review your additional "
"filters."
msgstr ""
"Za izbrane iskalne parametre ni bilo najdenih izdelkov.\n"
"\n"
"Uporabljeni filtri morda omejujejo rezultate. Za več rezultatov poskusite "
"izbrati več virov podatkov, razširiti časovni obseg ali izbrati večje "
"območje na karti. Preverite lahko tudi dodatne filtre."

msgid "VHR Europe 2024 Mosaic"
msgstr "VHR Europe 2024 Mosaic"

msgid "Red band"
msgstr "Rdeči kanal"

msgid "Green band"
msgstr "Zeleni kanal"

msgid "Blue band"
msgstr "Modri kanal"

msgid "Grey band"
msgstr "Sivi kanal"

msgid ""
"This dataset comprises one cloud-free Very High Resolution optical coverage "
"of 39 European States (EEA-39) including all islands of those countries "
"plus\n"
"the French Overseas Departments of French Guiana, Martinique, Guadeloupe, "
"Mayotte and Réunion but excluding French Overseas Territories. The area of\n"
"interest (~6 million square kilometres) is extended by a 4 km buffer over "
"the sea and a 500 m buffer over countries bordering the EEA-39 states.\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/optical-vhr-coverage-over-europe-"
"vhrimage2024)."
msgstr ""
"Ta zbirka podatkov vsebuje eno brezoblačno optično pokritost zelo visoke "
"ločljivosti 39 evropskih držav (EEA-39), vključno z vsemi otoki teh držav "
"ter\n"
"francoskimi čezmorskimi departmaji Francoska Gvajana, Martinik, Guadeloupe, "
"Mayotte in Réunion, vendar brez francoskih čezmorskih ozemelj. Območje\n"
"interesa (~6 milijonov kvadratnih kilometrov) je razširjeno za 4 km pas nad "
"morjem in 500 m pas nad državami, ki mejijo na države EEA-39.\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/optical-vhr-coverage-over-europe-"
"vhrimage2024)."

msgid ""
"This mosaic dataset, directly processed and delivered by the data provider, "
"comprises one cloud-free Very High Resolution optical coverage of 39 "
"European States (EEA-39) including all islands of those countries plus\n"
"the French Overseas Departments of French Guiana, Martinique, Guadeloupe, "
"Mayotte and Réunion but excluding French Overseas Territories. The area of\n"
"interest (~6 million square kilometres) is extended by a 4 km buffer over "
"the sea and a 500 m buffer over countries bordering the EEA-39 states.\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/optical-vhr-coverage-over-europe-"
"vhrimage2024)."
msgstr ""
"Ta mozaična zbirka podatkov, ki jo je neposredno obdelal in dostavil "
"ponudnik podatkov, vsebuje eno brezoblačno optično pokritost zelo visoke "
"ločljivosti 39 evropskih držav (EEA-39), vključno z vsemi otoki teh držav "
"ter\n"
"francoskimi čezmorskimi departmaji Francoska Gvajana, Martinik, Guadeloupe, "
"Mayotte in Réunion, vendar brez francoskih čezmorskih ozemelj. Območje\n"
"interesa (~6 milijonov kvadratnih kilometrov) je razširjeno za 4 km pas nad "
"morjem in 500 m pas nad državami, ki mejijo na države EEA-39.\n"
"Več informacij "
"[tukaj](https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/optical-vhr-coverage-over-europe-"
"vhrimage2024)."

msgid ""
"The Copernicus Contributing Missions (CCM) provide data that complements "
"the Copernicus Sentinel Missions and play a crucial role in Earth "
"observation.\n"
"These missions are conducted by ESA, its Member States, and international "
"third-party operators, and they offer very high to high resolution optical, "
"radar\n"
"and elevation model data. More "
"[info](https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/explore-data/data-collections/"
"copernicus-contributing-missions)."
msgstr ""
"Misije Copernicus Contributing Missions (CCM) zagotavljajo podatke, ki "
"dopolnjujejo misije Copernicus Sentinel in imajo ključno vlogo pri "
"opazovanju Zemlje.\n"
"Te misije izvajajo ESA, njene države članice in mednarodni tretji "
"operaterji ter ponujajo optične, radarske podatke in podatke digitalnega "
"modela višin\n"
"zelo visoke do visoke ločljivosti. Več "
"[informacij](https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/explore-data/data-collections/"
"copernicus-contributing-missions)."

